&lt;div class=&quot;separator&quot; style=&quot;clear: both; text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjW8xY0zA2bC4dE6fG8hI0jK2lM4nO6pQ8rS/s1600/IMG_20250809_190044.jpg&quot; style=&quot;margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;&quot;&gt;&lt;img border=&quot;0&quot; data-original-height=&quot;800&quot; data-original-width=&quot;1200&quot; height=&quot;213&quot; src=&quot;http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjW8xY0zA2bC4dE6fG8hI0jK2lM4nO6pQ8rS/s320/IMG_20250809_190044.jpg&quot; width=&quot;320&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Ten years ago this week I wrote my first post here, about a scarf with a dropped stitch I never fixed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Thank you to everyone who reads, comments and sends me pictures of what you have made. Here is to the next ten.&lt;/p&gt;</content><author><name>Ros Pengelly</name><uri>http://www.blogger.test/profile/09127364558120394471</uri><email>noreply@blogger.test</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.test/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><media:thumbnail xmlns:media='http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/' url='http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjW8xY0zA2bC4dE6fG8hI0jK2lM4nO6pQ8rS/s72-c/IMG_20250809_190044.jpg' height='72' width='72'/><thr:total>1</thr:total><link rel='replies' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/feeds/2093847561029384756/comments/default' title='Post Comments'/><link rel='replies' type='text/html' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/2025/08/ten-years-of-wool-and-waves.html#comment-form' title='1 Comments'/><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/2093847561029384756'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/2093847561029384756'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/2025/08/ten-years-of-wool-and-waves.html' title='Ten years of Wool and Waves'/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-4827364510293847561.post-8392017465839201746</id><published>2023-03-19T15:50:00.000Z</published><updated>2023-03-19T15:50:00.000Z</updated><category scheme='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#kind' term='http://schemas.google.com/blogger/2008/kind#post'/><category scheme='http://www.blogger.com/atom/ns#' term='Dyeing'/><category scheme='http://www.blogger.com/atom/ns#' term='Yarn'/><title type='text'>Dyeing yarn with gorse flowers</title><content type='html'>&lt;div class=&quot;separator&quot; style=&quot;clear: both; text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhV7wX9yZ1aB3cD5eF7gH9iJ1kL3mN5oP7qR/s1600/IMG_20230318_165502.jpg&quot; style=&quot;margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;&quot;&gt;&lt;img border=&quot;0&quot; data-original-height=&quot;800&quot; data-original-width=&quot;1200&quot; height=&quot;213&quot; src=&quot;http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhV7wX9yZ1aB3cD5eF7gH9iJ1kL3mN5oP7qR/s320/IMG_20230318_165502.jpg&quot; width=&quot;320&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The gorse is out on the cliffs, so I picked a carrier bag of flowers and had a go at dyeing with it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Simmered for an hour with alum as a mordant, it gave a lovely soft yellow. Wear gloves when you pick, it is prickly stuff.&lt;/p&gt;</content><author><name>Ros Pengelly</name><uri>http://www.blogger.test/profile/09127364558120394471</uri><email>noreply@blogger.test</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.test/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><media:thumbnail xmlns:media='http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/' url='http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhV7wX9yZ1aB3cD5eF7gH9iJ1kL3mN5oP7qR/s72-c/IMG_20230318_165502.jpg' height='72' width='72'/><thr:total>0</thr:total><link rel='replies' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/feeds/8392017465839201746/comments/default' title='Post Comments'/><link rel='replies' type='text/html' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/2023/03/dyeing-yarn-with-gorse-flowers.html#comment-form' title='0 Comments'/><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/8392017465839201746'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/8392017465839201746'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/2023/03/dyeing-yarn-with-gorse-flowers.html' title='Dyeing yarn with gorse flowers'/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-4827364510293847561.post-6574839201928374650</id><published>2021-11-28T10:15:00.000Z</published><updated>2021-11-28T10:15:00.000Z</updated><category scheme='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#kind' term='http://schemas.google.com/blogger/2008/kind#post'/><category scheme='http://www.blogger.com/atom/ns#' term='Patterns'/><category scheme='http://www.blogger.com/atom/ns#' term='Christmas'/><title type='text'>Christmas jumper pattern, free to download</title><content type='html'>&lt;p&gt;My Christmas jumper pattern is finished and tested, and it is free for anyone who wants it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It is a simple raglan with a fair isle yoke of holly and snowflakes, sized for children and adults. Email me and I will send you the pattern.&lt;/p&gt;</content><author><name>Ros Pengelly</name><uri>http://www.blogger.test/profile/09127364558120394471</uri><email>noreply@blogger.test</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.test/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:total>0</thr:total><link rel='replies' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/feeds/6574839201928374650/comments/default' title='Post Comments'/><link rel='replies' type='text/html' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/2021/11/christmas-jumper-pattern-free-to.html#comment-form' title='0 Comments'/><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/6574839201928374650'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/6574839201928374650'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/2021/11/christmas-jumper-pattern-free-to.html' title='Christmas jumper pattern, free to download'/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-4827364510293847561.post-1029384756102938475</id><published>2020-04-05T17:30:00.000+01:00</published><updated>2020-04-05T17:30:00.000+01:00</updated><category scheme='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#kind' term='http://schemas.google.com/blogger/2008/kind#post'/><category scheme='http://www.blogger.com/atom/ns#' term='Blankets'/><title type='text'>Lockdown blanket, square by square</title><content type='html'>&lt;div class=&quot;separator&quot; style=&quot;clear: both; text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEiU6vW8xY0zA2bC4dE6fG8hI0jK2lM4nO6pQ/s1600/IMG_20200405_120318.jpg&quot; style=&quot;margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;&quot;&gt;&lt;img border=&quot;0&quot; data-original-height=&quot;800&quot; data-original-width=&quot;1200&quot; height=&quot;213&quot; src=&quot;http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEiU6vW8xY0zA2bC4dE6fG8hI0jK2lM4nO6pQ/s320/IMG_20200405_120318.jpg&quot; width=&quot;320&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;A square a day while we are all stuck indoors. Forty-two squares so far, every one from the oddments basket.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;If you want to join in, any double knitting yarn will do. Cast on 30 stitches and knit until it is square.&lt;/p&gt;</content><author><name>Ros Pengelly</name><uri>http://www.blogger.test/profile/09127364558120394471</uri><email>noreply@blogger.test</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.test/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><media:thumbnail xmlns:media='http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/' url='http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEiU6vW8xY0zA2bC4dE6fG8hI0jK2lM4nO6pQ/s72-c/IMG_20200405_120318.jpg' height='72' width='72'/><thr:total>0</thr:total><link rel='replies' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/feeds/1029384756102938475/comments/default' title='Post Comments'/><link rel='replies' type='text/html' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/2020/04/lockdown-blanket-square-by-square.html#comment-form' title='0 Comments'/><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/1029384756102938475'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/1029384756102938475'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/2020/04/lockdown-blanket-square-by-square.html' title='Lockdown blanket, square by square'/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-4827364510293847561.post-9928374650192837465</id><published>2019-09-22T12:05:00.000+01:00</published><updated>2019-09-22T12:05:00.000+01:00</updated><category scheme='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#kind' term='http://schemas.google.com/blogger/2008/kind#post'/><category scheme='http://www.blogger.com/atom/ns#' term='Out and about'/><category scheme='http://www.blogger.com/atom/ns#' term='Yarn'/><title type='text'>Wool shop crawl in Falmouth</title><content type='html'>&lt;div class=&quot;separator&quot; style=&quot;clear: both; text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgT5uV7wX9yZ1aB3cD5eF7gH9iJ1kL3mN5oP/s1600/IMG_20190921_141530.jpg&quot; style=&quot;margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;&quot;&gt;&lt;img border=&quot;0&quot; data-original-height=&quot;800&quot; data-original-width=&quot;1200&quot; height=&quot;213&quot; src=&quot;http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgT5uV7wX9yZ1aB3cD5eF7gH9iJ1kL3mN5oP/s320/IMG_20190921_141530.jpg&quot; width=&quot;320&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Jo and I spent Saturday going round three wool shops in Falmouth, with a pasty stop in the middle.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;I came home with far too much British wool and a skein of hand-dyed blue that I have no plan for at all.&lt;/p&gt;</content><author><name>Ros Pengelly</name><uri>http://www.blogger.test/profile/09127364558120394471</uri><email>noreply@blogger.test</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.test/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><media:thumbnail xmlns:media='http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/' url='http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgT5uV7wX9yZ1aB3cD5eF7gH9iJ1kL3mN5oP/s72-c/IMG_20190921_141530.jpg' height='72' width='72'/><thr:total>0</thr:total><link rel='replies' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/feeds/9928374650192837465/comments/default' title='Post Comments'/><link rel='replies' type='text/html' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/2019/09/wool-shop-crawl-in-falmouth.html#comment-form' title='0 Comments'/><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/9928374650192837465'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/9928374650192837465'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/2019/09/wool-shop-crawl-in-falmouth.html' title='Wool shop crawl in Falmouth'/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-4827364510293847561.post-5583920174652839104</id><published>2018-02-11T14:25:00.000Z</published><updated>2018-02-11T14:25:00.000Z</updated><category scheme='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#kind' term='http://schemas.google.com/blogger/2008/kind#post'/><category scheme='http://www.blogger.com/atom/ns#' term='Ganseys'/><category scheme='http://www.blogger.com/atom/ns#' term='Patterns'/><title type='text'>A gansey for Dad</title><content type='html'>&lt;div class=&quot;separator&quot; style=&quot;clear: both; text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjR8tU2vW4xY6zA1bC3dE5fG7hI9jK0lM2nO/s1600/IMG_20180210_112245.jpg&quot; style=&quot;margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;&quot;&gt;&lt;img border=&quot;0&quot; data-original-height=&quot;800&quot; data-original-width=&quot;1200&quot; height=&quot;213&quot; src=&quot;http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjR8tU2vW4xY6zA1bC3dE5fG7hI9jK0lM2nO/s320/IMG_20180210_112245.jpg&quot; width=&quot;320&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fourteen months, two false starts and one very patient father later, the gansey is done.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It is knitted in the round in navy five-ply, with the old Polperro pattern across the chest. Dad says he will wear it on the boat, which is the highest compliment.&lt;/p&gt;</content><author><name>Ros Pengelly</name><uri>http://www.blogger.test/profile/09127364558120394471</uri><email>noreply@blogger.test</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.test/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><media:thumbnail xmlns:media='http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/' url='http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjR8tU2vW4xY6zA1bC3dE5fG7hI9jK0lM2nO/s72-c/IMG_20180210_112245.jpg' height='72' width='72'/><thr:total>1</thr:total><link rel='replies' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/feeds/5583920174652839104/comments/default' title='Post Comments'/><link rel='replies' type='text/html' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/2018/02/a-gansey-for-dad.html#comment-form' title='1 Comments'/><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/5583920174652839104'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/5583920174652839104'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/2018/02/a-gansey-for-dad.html' title='A gansey for Dad'/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-4827364510293847561.post-3301928475610293847</id><published>2017-06-04T19:10:00.000+01:00</published><updated>2017-06-04T19:10:00.000+01:00</updated><category scheme='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#kind' term='http://schemas.google.com/blogger/2008/kind#post'/><category scheme='http://www.blogger.com/atom/ns#' term='Out and about'/><title type='text'>Knitting on the beach</title><content type='html'>&lt;p&gt;Took the shawl down to Porthmeor this evening and got a whole lace repeat done before the tide came in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Top tip: wooden needles and sand do not mix. Bamboo ones are fine. Ask me how I know.&lt;/p&gt;</content><author><name>Ros Pengelly</name><uri>http://www.blogger.test/profile/09127364558120394471</uri><email>noreply@blogger.test</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.test/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><thr:total>0</thr:total><link rel='replies' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/feeds/3301928475610293847/comments/default' title='Post Comments'/><link rel='replies' type='text/html' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/2017/06/knitting-on-beach.html#comment-form' title='0 Comments'/><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/3301928475610293847'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/3301928475610293847'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/2017/06/knitting-on-beach.html' title='Knitting on the beach'/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-4827364510293847561.post-7710293847561029384</id><published>2017-01-15T16:42:00.000Z</published><updated>2017-01-15T16:42:00.000Z</updated><category scheme='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#kind' term='http://schemas.google.com/blogger/2008/kind#post'/><category scheme='http://www.blogger.com/atom/ns#' term='Socks'/><title type='text'>My first pair of socks</title><content type='html'>&lt;div class=&quot;separator&quot; style=&quot;clear: both; text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhQ2vT8kLmN4pR7sW1xY3zB6cD9eF0gH2jK5/s1600/IMG_20170114_153012.jpg&quot; style=&quot;margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;&quot;&gt;&lt;img border=&quot;0&quot; data-original-height=&quot;800&quot; data-original-width=&quot;1200&quot; height=&quot;213&quot; src=&quot;http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhQ2vT8kLmN4pR7sW1xY3zB6cD9eF0gH2jK5/s320/IMG_20170114_153012.jpg&quot; width=&quot;320&quot; /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Well, I did it. After three years of scarves I finally turned a heel, and then did it again so there are two of them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;They are toe-up, in a sock yarn from the shop in St Just, and the second one is a bit tighter than the first. Nobody will notice when they are on my feet.&lt;/p&gt;</content><author><name>Ros Pengelly</name><uri>http://www.blogger.test/profile/09127364558120394471</uri><email>noreply@blogger.test</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.test/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><media:thumbnail xmlns:media='http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/' url='http://blogger.googleusercontent.test/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhQ2vT8kLmN4pR7sW1xY3zB6cD9eF0gH2jK5/s72-c/IMG_20170114_153012.jpg' height='72' width='72'/><thr:total>1</thr:total><link rel='replies' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/feeds/7710293847561029384/comments/default' title='Post Comments'/><link rel='replies' type='text/html' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/2017/01/my-first-pair-of-socks.html#comment-form' title='1 Comments'/><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/7710293847561029384'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/7710293847561029384'/><link rel='alternate' type='text/html' href='http://woolandwaves.blogspot.test/2017/01/my-first-pair-of-socks.html' title='My first pair of socks'/></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-4827364510293847561.post-4410293847561920384</id><published>2024-02-02T21:14:00.000Z</published><updated>2024-02-02T21:14:00.000Z</updated><category scheme='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#kind' term='http://schemas.google.com/blogger/2008/kind#post'/><category scheme='http://www.blogger.com/atom/ns#' term='Patterns'/><title type='text'>Rock Pool shawl, a pattern review</title><content type='html'>&lt;p&gt;Half written. The Rock Pool shawl pattern is lovely but the chart for row 37 has a mistake, need to check with the designer before I say so.&lt;/p&gt;</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/4410293847561920384'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/4410293847561920384'/><author><name>Ros Pengelly</name><uri>http://www.blogger.test/profile/09127364558120394471</uri><email>noreply@blogger.test</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.test/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><app:control xmlns:app='http://purl.org/atom/app#'><app:draft>yes</app:draft></app:control></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-4827364510293847561.post-7720394857610293845</id><published>2026-09-30T20:02:00.000+01:00</published><updated>2026-09-30T20:02:00.000+01:00</updated><category scheme='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#kind' term='http://schemas.google.com/blogger/2008/kind#post'/><title type='text'>Selling my spinning wheel?</title><content type='html'>&lt;p&gt;Not sure about this one yet. Thinking of selling the Ashford wheel as I never use it.&lt;/p&gt;</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/7720394857610293845'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/posts/default/7720394857610293845'/><author><name>Ros Pengelly</name><uri>http://www.blogger.test/profile/09127364558120394471</uri><email>noreply@blogger.test</email><gd:image rel='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail' width='16' height='16' src='http://img1.blogblog.test/img/b16-rounded.gif'/></author><app:control xmlns:app='http://purl.org/atom/app#'><app:draft>yes</app:draft></app:control></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-4827364510293847561.post-1029384756473829100</id><published>2017-01-16T09:12:00.000Z</published><updated>2017-01-16T09:12:00.000Z</updated><category scheme='http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#kind' term='http://schemas.google.com/blogger/2008/kind#comment'/><title type='text'>Lovely socks! Nobody ever notices the...</title><content type='html'>Lovely socks! Nobody ever notices the second one is tighter, honestly.</content><link rel='edit' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/7710293847561029384/comments/default/1029384756473829100'/><link rel='self' type='application/atom+xml' href='http://www.blogger.test/feeds/4827364510293847561/7710293847561029384/comments/default/1029384756473829100'/><link re